{"delay_ms":0,"frame":{"classification":"C1","ledger_seq":null,"ns":[],"payload":{"body":"BOIL WATER ADVISORY for customers of SGW in the Cedarfall water zone. Issued: [date and time of release]. Because Hurricane Helene may cause a loss of water pressure in this zone, SGW is issuing this precautionary advisory before landfall. Customers in the Cedarfall zone should boil water used for drinking and cooking. Bring water to a rolling boil for one minute, then let it cool before use. Use boiled or bottled water for drinking, making ice, brushing teeth, washing dishes and preparing food. SGW is working with the South Carolina Department of Environmental Services (SCDES). We will lift this boil water advisory when test results show the water is safe. For questions call SGW Water at [phone]. We will provide the next update at: [time].","clause":"SC DES, Boil Water Notices and Advisories (2024): advisory prior to a hurricane making landfall","clause_id":"SC-A2","kind":"bwa_notice_draft","rule_id":"rule.sc_bwa_pre_landfall","template":"WQC 07.120 Rev C Attachment A","title":"BOIL WATER ADVISORY for customers of SGW in the Cedarfall water zone","zone_id":"WZ-PS17-CEDARFALL"},"run_id":"run-7172093948c6","run_mode":"replay","scenario_time":null,"seq":33,"ts":"2026-11-22T11:53:21.857165Z","type":"artifact","v":1},"id":"run:run-7172093948c6.1795348399.33"}
